  > logger.go::New #b9fc6b1129d8
#c2[overview,i5] Entries encapsulate contextual fields and data, creating non-mutating clones when chaining field additions and borrowing pooled instances managed by an internal sync pool.
  > entry.go:44-46 #36ec58c2b314
  > entry.go::Dup #41f846b1d1af
  > exported.go:67-70 #eb0e73a97c21
  > logger.go::releaseEntry #10d1f8c1912d
  > logger.go::WithField #57d11ca154a1
#c3[overview,i5] Logging severity is controlled by seven granular levels, accessed via atomic level checks, case-insensitive string parsing, and optional function-evaluated logging methods.
  > README.md::"Level logging" #6386bc0ba3b9
  > exported.go::InfoFn #917b63dd546c
  > logger.go::SetLevel #8cbddc44ce64
  > logrus.go:100-119 #8d709a6f7fc7
  > logrus.go::parseLevel #3deb048b78cd
#c4[overview,i5] Dedicated panic and fatal methods execute hooks and writes before either raising a Go panic or invoking registered exit handlers sequentially prior to process termination.
  > README.md::"Level logging" #6386bc0ba3b9
  > README.md::"Fatal handlers" #c68021be4d42
