  = bufio.MaxScanTokenSize (64KB).
  > writer.go::writerScanner #bd177246b1ed
?p22 What logging level is assigned to lines written through logger.Writer()?
  = info
  > README.md::"Logger as an `io.Writer`" #43c8882c77fb
?p23 How does DeferExitHandler order a newly added handler relative to existing handlers?
  = It prepends the handler to the list.
  > alt_exit.go::DeferExitHandler #ad6fd8ee9de6
?p24 What type does the sync.Pool New function in defaultPool return?
  = new(bytes.Buffer)
  > buffer_pool.go::func #20cc811f5343
?p25 What is the simplest way to use Logrus?
  = The package-level exported logger.
  > doc.go:4 #a0b77d449162
?p26 What exit code is passed to Logger.Exit when Entry.Fatal is called?
  = 1
  > entry.go::Fatal #ee120caa93cb
?p27 Which top-level function returns the package-level Logger pointer?
  = StandardLogger()
  > exported.go::StandardLogger #3aa8295fcb06
?p28 How are colliding user-provided keys modified by prefixFieldClashes in data?
  = They are prefixed with "fields." and deleted from their original key names.
  > formatter.go::prefixFieldClashes #1e5a62318444
?p29 Are hooks fired asynchronously in separate goroutines by default?
  = No, they are not fired in a goroutine or worker channel.
  > hooks.go:4-5 #5116b2da078d
?p30 How does JSONFormatter represent error values from Entry.Data?
  = By calling v.Error() to store the error's string message.
  > json_formatter.go::Format #969daa51b43a
